A||||8||Raydar||V8 Engine Kits||||5||
Z||000000||Raydar||03-28-2000||12:34 PM||||In the past few weeks, I've run across several V8 swap kits, from various vendors. Most (except for Archie's) seem to be similar to the Zumalt kit. It seems that all of these kits use solid axles -no CV joints. I have heard that Archie's LT1 and LS1 kit also requires axle replacement. Are these solid axles, also? <BR>Aren't CV joints required?!? Or is that just a carry-over from the FWD drivetrain? Is there enough "play" where the splines plug into the trans to let the axles move up and down with the wheels? Seems like this would be awfully hard on the tranny bearings and seals. Maybe even the case. Am I missing something?<P>Thanks. <P>Steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||HarryG||03-28-2000||12:49 PM||||I think you're probably seeing ads which mention "axles" but only show pictures of the axle shaft, minus the CV joints. You still need the joints.||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||03-28-2000||01:01 PM||||That's what I've been trying to get the answer, too.  I bought a nice used LT1 because I wanted a fuel-injected engine to avoid problems with the emissions zealots in Wisconsin.  Also for driveability.  I was going to use v8archie's kit because he said any small block chevy would fit.  When I went to his open house, he said due to its extra length, the engine would have to be moved 2 inches toward the driver's side.  I e-mailed to ask then what happens to the axles because he said his sbc conversion retains the stock axles.  I haven't heard back yet.  I'd love to know the answer because I'm ready to go with a conversion.  Coyote, don't you work there?  Can you help us out with an answer?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||coyote||03-28-2000||03:29 PM||||When i refer to axles, i am talking about the part between the CV joints. You will need to replace that part. You still use the CV joints. LT1 axles are shorter on the drivers side and longer on the passanger side and will have to be made.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||03-28-2000||03:37 PM||||Thanks for the replies, guys.<BR>Coyote, Does the LT1 kit still place moving parts in the wheelwell? Or does the 2" shift to the left remedy that? That's the only problem I've ever had with Archie's kit. I understand that there are many conversions configured exactly like that, but still...<P>Thanks, again!<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||03-28-2000||07:58 PM||||The LT1 engine has to moved so that the LT1 water pump will fit inside the frame wells!<P>This water pump is driven off the cam (or cam drive) not an external belt like the earlier SBC engines.  <P>So the answer about the "stuff" in the wheelwell is "NO!"<P>The problem is you have to notch the LEFT side frame to clear the transaxle and you have to use a shorter axle on the left and a longer axle on the right (like the Zumalt and clone kits).<P>You will use your stock CV joints and mount them on the new axles.  If you were to take your current CV joints off, your axles would look like what you have seen in the pictures!<P>BTW, that is why I am doing a TPI swap instead of a LT1 swap, so I don't have to move the engine to the left and use aftermarket axles!  I still will have the electronic fuel injection but will build it on a earlier model SBC engine.  I also, will not have any "stuff" in the wheelwell since I will be using an electric water pump that is rated almost as high a flow as a stock pump is! (37 gal/minute)<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 03-28-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||03-29-2000||04:10 AM||||COULD YOU POST LINKS TO THE OTHER MAKERS OF KITS BESIDES ARCHIE.  ARCHIE IS THE ONLY ONE YOU CAN FIND ON THE NET.  I hate caps lock <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000007||Raydar||03-29-2000||10:16 AM||||Paul, and others, <BR>Thanks for the info. Exactly what I was looking for.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Dan, <BR>I'll see what I can find. Don't have most of my links here at work. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-29-2000).]||||reg||1
